From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leo Lobato <leo@lobato.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:59:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: accesses beside an inaccessible page stop being stepped
 once they run hot (Wine patch 0975)

prospero-win 959b2d1 (#739), after the v0.2.0 PC5 builds on, picked onto
PC5's patches. Upstream's Wine patch 0986 is 0975 here: PC5's own 0986
has that number.

- Patch 0974 single-steps an access that faults only because a protected page shares its 16 KiB host page. It stopped
  doing that only for writes beside a read-only page, so an access beside an inaccessible page was stepped forever.
- Every stepped access is now counted, reads too. After 256 on one host page, a write beside a read-only page is still
  reported, and any other access gives the host page the union of its pages' protections until a protection in it
  changes.
- `tests/wine_subpage_protect.c` checks that 20,000 reads and writes beside an inaccessible page stop faulting, and that
  the next protection change faults again.
